WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.700
When Hollywood does any kind of movie or TV
show about counterterrorism, about spying,

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.490
they tend to have Jack Bauer doing something
dramatic.

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:08.029
They have James Bond doing something dramatic.

00:00:08.029 --> 00:00:10.940
They have Carrie Mathison doing something
emotional and dramatic.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.929
You said you had information about an attack.

00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:16.580
But it’s, like, one person, in one dangerous
place, doing one powerful thing.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.440
And that’s not the way the world actually
works.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:25.679
In reality, the US relies on a web of intelligence-sharing
agreements with other countries.

00:00:25.679 --> 00:00:30.390
The best known is the Five Eyes agreement
between the US, Canada, the United Kingdom,

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.099
New Zealand, and Australia.

00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:36.520
But the US also gets intel from countries
that are geographically closer to terrorism

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:37.520
hot spots.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.290
Jordan, Saudi Arabia, the Emirates , Turkey,
Israel,

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:45.660
These countries often have agents undercover
inside groups like ISIS.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:48.020
They get something valuable, they trust us
with it.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:52.350
That could be an intercept of a phone call,
drone imagery showing somebody that one country

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:53.350
is looking for.

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:55.000
It could be a plot.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.879
This was the case in 2010, when intelligence
sharing between the US and six other countries

00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:05.450
stopped an al-Qaeda plot to bomb two cargo
planes en route to the US.

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:09.500
And what makes it all work, what kind of greases
that relationship, is trust.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.370
They believe that if they tell us a secret,
that it’s safe.

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:16.740
One of the most important of these intelligence-sharing
relationships is the one between the United

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.100
States and the Israelis.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:22.710
So, when the Israelis found out about a specific
threat from ISIS, that they planned to use

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:26.070
laptops to bomb airplanes,
The New York Times reports that the Israelis

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:30.760
shared that information with the US, with
the understanding it would stay secret.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:34.740
But the Washington Post reports that President
Trump shared that information with the Russian

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.260
foreign minister during his visit to the US.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:42.430
And in doing so, he seriously jeopardized
that relationship with the Israelis.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:47.610
To understand why, you have to back up a little
bit and look at what Russia is doing in Syria.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:51.960
President Trump has said Russia is a key ally
in the fight against ISIS there.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:55.230
Trump: I say it's better to get along with
Russia than not.

00:01:55.230 --> 00:02:00.680
And if Russia helps us in the fight against
ISIS, which is a major fight, and Islamic

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.131
terrorism all over the world — major fight —that's a good thing.

00:02:04.131 --> 00:02:07.240
The problem is that, in Syria, Russia’s
goal is not to fight ISIS.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.259
Russia’s goal is to protect Bashar al-Assad.

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:13.520
Russia fights ISIS only insofar as it sees
ISIS as a threat to Bashar A\al-Assad.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:17.150
And one of Russia’s main partners in this
objective is Iran,

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:20.850
who the Israelis consider to be their greatest
threat in the region.

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:23.640
The greatest danger that we face

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.080
of the hatred for the Jewish people and the

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.520
Jewish state, comes from the East.

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:32.950
It comes from Iran.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:37.920
For months, Israeli spies have expressed this
fear that any intelligence they shared with

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.730
the US could end up, via Russia, in the hands
of the Iranians.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:45.220
And Now those fears have been confirmed.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:48.970
If they no longer trust the CIA, that means
that the plot that might have otherwise been

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:51.830
stopped or disrupted potentially happens.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:55.310
Because they don’t trust that if they tell
it to us, that it won’t go to an enemy of

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:56.310
theirs.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.400
And it’s not just Israel.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:02.960
Now other allies may become wary of sharing
intelligence with the US.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:06.990
Without trust, these intelligence-sharing
relationships break down.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:11.620
And without these relationships, it’s harder
for US intelligence officials to do the very

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:16.879
thing Trump says he wants to accomplish: defeat
ISIS and disrupt terror plots.

